From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:14:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2: add the HLG transfer function

The V4L2 transfer function enum ends at SMPTE ST 2084, and the core
resets any other value to V4L2_XFER_FUNC_DEFAULT on VIDIOC_S_FMT before
a driver sees it, so a client cannot state hybrid log-gamma on any
queue and an HDR encoder cannot tell the stream's transfer function to
its device. HLG is a transfer function in its own right, ITU-R BT.2100,
and the Virtio video encoder carries the colorimetry of the raw queue
as the client states it.

The enum gains V4L2_XFER_FUNC_HLG, value 8, which is also what
V4L2_XFER_FUNC_LAST validates against. Upstream has no value for HLG;
this one is a local extension of the UAPI, and if upstream adds one it
replaces this number here and in the wire table of the Virtio video
device (virtio_video_v4l2_ids.h), which names the same value.
---
 include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h b/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h
index becd08fdbddb857f8f2bf205d2164dc6e20e80b2..d3937453b2256924f9a3b152ea3cdcef11c8b8da 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/videodev2.h
@@ -299,6 +299,12 @@ enum v4l2_xfer_func {
 	V4L2_XFER_FUNC_NONE        = 5,
 	V4L2_XFER_FUNC_DCI_P3      = 6,
 	V4L2_XFER_FUNC_SMPTE2084   = 7,
+	/*
+	 * ITU-R BT.2100 hybrid log-gamma. Upstream V4L2 has no value for it;
+	 * this one is a local extension. If upstream adds HLG, adopt its
+	 * value here and in the Virtio video wire table.
+	 */
+	V4L2_XFER_FUNC_HLG         = 8,
 #ifdef __KERNEL__
 	/*
 	 * Largest supported transfer function value, assigned by the compiler,
